# Line endings.
#
# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, on every platform. Without
# this, a Windows checkout converts them to CRLF (the GitHub Windows runners have
# core.autocrlf=true), and the formatting gate — `gofmt -l .` — then reports every
# Go file in the tree, because gofmt compares bytes. The CI job that runs that gate
# on Windows also pins this for itself (see .github/workflows/ci.yml); this file is
# what protects every other Windows checkout, including a contributor's.
#
# `text=auto` means Git decides by content, so a binary file added later is left
# alone without an entry here.
* text=auto eol=lf
